Here is an issue:

Issue Title: [BUG] KeyError in Mem0Storage when using local_mem0_config (OSS Memory) and missing params

Description:
### Description

When using Mem0 with CrewAI via the local_mem0_config (OSS Memory) pathway, a KeyError is thrown in Mem0Storage's search method if the params dictionary does not contain certain keys (e.g. metadata, output_format, version). This is caused by the following code block:

```
if isinstance(self.memory, Memory):
    del params["metadata"], params["version"], params['output_format']
    if params.get("run_id"):
        del params["run_id"]
If any of those fields are missing from params, Python raises a KeyError. This is a bug because the code should check existence before deletion to be robust.
```

My Crew Code:

```
@crew
def crew(self) -> Crew:
    return Crew(
        agents=self.agents,
        tasks=self.tasks,
        llm=get_llm_model("llama4-scout-17b"),
        process=Process.sequential,  # Purely sequential for now
        verbose=True,
        memory=True,
        memory_config={
            "provider": "mem0",
            "config": {
                "user_id": "john",
                "local_mem0_config": {
                    "vector_store": {
                        "provider": "pgvector",
                        "config": {"dbname":"memory","host": "localhost","user":"memory","password":"memory", "port": 5432}
                    },
                    "llm": {
                        "provider": "vllm",
                        "config": {"vllm_base_url": "http://localhost/v1","temperature":0.1,"api_key":"EMPTY", "model": "llama4-scout-17b"}
                    },
                    "embedder": {
                        "provider": "huggingface",
                        "config": { "model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"}
                    }
                },
                "infer": True
            },
            "user_memory": {}
        }
    )
```


### Steps to Reproduce

- Run your workflow, e.g. with Research().crew().kickoff(inputs={"topic": data,"user_id":"test"}).
- Observe the error.

### Expected behavior

The workflow should run without errors, even if some parameters (such as "metadata", "output_format", "version") are missing from the params dictionary.
Memory operations should proceed without raising a KeyError.

### Screenshots/Code snippets

```
@crew
def crew(self) -> Crew:
    return Crew(
        agents=self.agents,
        tasks=self.tasks,
        llm=get_llm_model("llama4-scout-17b"),
        process=Process.sequential,  # Purely sequential for now
        verbose=True,
        memory=True,
        memory_config={
            "provider": "mem0",
            "config": {
                "user_id": "john",
                "local_mem0_config": {
                    "vector_store": {
                        "provider": "pgvector",
                        "config": {"dbname":"memory","host": "localhost","user":"memory","password":"memory", "port": 5432}
                    },
                    "llm": {
                        "provider": "vllm",
                        "config": {"vllm_base_url": "http://localhost/v1","temperature":0.1,"api_key":"EMPTY", "model": "llama4-scout-17b"}
                    },
                    "embedder": {
                        "provider": "huggingface",
                        "config": { "model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"}
                    }
                },
                "infer": True
            },
            "user_memory": {}
        }
    )
```

Run Code
`Research().crew().kickoff(inputs={"topic": data,"user_id":"test"})`

Error traceback
```
KeyError: 'metadata'
  File .../crewai/memory/storage/mem0_storage.py, line 125, in search
    del params["metadata"], params["output_format"]
```

### Operating System

Ubuntu 20.04

### Python Version

3.10

### crewAI Version

0.152.0

### crewAI Tools Version

-

### Virtual Environment

Venv

### Evidence

Error output above.
Code samples provided.
[mem0_storage.py source code](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/src/crewai/memory/storage/mem0_storage.py)
Related tests: [tests/storage/test_mem0_storage.py](https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/main/tests/storage/test_mem0_storage.py)


### Possible Solution

Replace the block with:

Python
if isinstance(self.memory, Memory):
    for key in ["metadata", "version", "output_format"]:
        if key in params:
            del params[key]
    if "run_id" in params:
        del params["run_id"]
This will prevent KeyError and make the code more robust.

### Additional context

The config structure follows the docs and examples; this is not a user error.
Anyone using local_mem0_config with the OSS Memory backend can encounter this issue if those keys are missing from params.
